+---
+
+### Preserve bounded bins
+
+```python
+age = pl.col("age").fill_nan(None)  # for a Float64 source column
+age_group = (
+    pl.when(age.is_between(0, 120, closed="right"))
+    .then(age.bin_intervals(
+        [17, 24, 34, 44, 54],
+        labels=["0-17", "17-24", "24-34", "34-44", "44-54", "54-120"],
+        right_closed=True,
+    ))
+    .otherwise(None)
+    .alias("age_group")
+)
+```
+
+This preserves pandas' default excluded lower edge and included upper edge for
+these explicit bins. Verify exact edges, adjacent values, outliers, nulls and NaN;
+match categorical representation separately when downstream consumers require it.
+Do not add `fill_nan` blindly to a non-floating source dtype. Quantile bins also
+need explicit checks for ties, duplicate edges, interpolation and null handling;
+similarly named methods do not establish pandas equivalence.
 
